<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I, Duke of Anhalt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1831–1904</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-iv-duke-of-anhalt">Leopold IV Frederick</a> as duke of Anhalt in 1871 and reigned until his death. Anhalt had been reunited under his father in 1863, and under Frederick it was a member state of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>. He was followed by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-grand-duke-of-baden">Frederick II</a>, and the duchy lasted until the German revolution of 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-i-duke-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="Frederick I, Duke of Anhalt" width="209" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_I_Anhalt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
